% holding-blocked: Replace the discovery search with an authorized link to Ilê Aiyê's own recording of "Que Bloco É Esse?" and confirm the album pairing (Canto Negro, 1984). A Grade 4 teacher must trial the syn-co-pa against the clapped ostinato, the accents and the lyric fit; a second score reader must check the two-part notation; an Afro-Brazilian or Bahia music educator must review the bloco afro context. The title was changed from "Bahia Signal" so the piece does not claim a place or tradition it does not come from; the lead should confirm the new title.
